cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sekaisen in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "sekaisen: a durable pipeline engine for AI agents in external harnesses"
abstract: >-
  sekaisen runs multi-stage work across AI agents that live in an external
  harness. Each pipeline is one YAML state machine. The engine dispatches a
  turn and returns at once, and the run resumes when the agent completes its
  stage with one of the declared outcomes. Runs survive restarts, every step
  is written to an append-only transition log, definitions are checked before
  a run, every path can be simulated on a virtual clock, and a scheduler
  treats agents and usage limits as scarce.
authors:
